Why it failed: GitHub's /releases/latest HTML page lazy-loads release assets dynamically, so scraping the HTML returned an empty link and wget saved an empty/404 file instead of the real Ghidra .zip or Bytecode Viewer .jar.
Query the GitHub Releases API (api.github.com) built entirely from split variables (so your browser extension never rewrites api.github.com or .zip/.jar URLs) to fetch and install both Ghidra and Bytecode Viewer:
bash
PROTO="https"
API_HOST="api.github"
TLD="com"

# 1. Install Ghidra via GitHub API
rm -rf /tmp/ghidra_dl && mkdir -p /tmp/ghidra_dl && cd /tmp/ghidra_dl && \
GHIDRA_API="${PROTO}://${API_HOST}.${TLD}/repos/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/releases/latest" && \
GHIDRA_URL=$(curl -s "$GHIDRA_API" | grep -oE 'https://[^"]+PUBLIC_[0-9]+\.zip' | head -n 1) && \
echo "Downloading Ghidra: $GHIDRA_URL" && \
wget -O ghidra.zip "$GHIDRA_URL" && \
unzip -oq ghidra.zip && \
sudo rm -rf /opt/ghidra && \
sudo mv ghidra_*_PUBLIC /opt/ghidra && \
sudo ln -sf /opt/ghidra/ghidraRun /usr/local/bin/ghidraRun && \
sudo ln -sf /opt/ghidra/ghidraRun /usr/local/bin/ghidra && \
cd ~ && rm -rf /tmp/ghidra_dl

# 2. Install Bytecode Viewer via GitHub API
sudo mkdir -p /opt/bytecode-viewer && \
BCV_API="${PROTO}://${API_HOST}.${TLD}/repos/Konloch/bytecode-viewer/releases/latest" && \
BCV_URL=$(curl -s "$BCV_API" | grep -oE 'https://[^"]+Bytecode-Viewer-[0-9.]+\.jar' | head -n 1) && \
echo "Downloading Bytecode Viewer: $BCV_URL" && \
sudo wget -O /opt/bytecode-viewer/Bytecode-Viewer.jar "$BCV_URL" && \
sudo tee /usr/local/bin/bytecode-viewer > /dev/null << 'EOF'
#!/usr/bin/env bash
java -jar /opt/bytecode-viewer/Bytecode-Viewer.jar "$@"
EOF
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/bytecode-viewer
Use code with caution.

